# GitHub releases

When creating or updating a `v*` tag / GitHub Release for this repo:

1. **Always set a real title and body** — do not leave the softprops / `generate_release_notes` stub (`**Full Changelog**: …` only).
2. **Match prior release shape** (see `v0.5.3` / `v0.6.0` / `v0.6.1`):
   - Title: `X.Y.Z — short summary`
   - Intro line (new sidecar / Python-only / etc.) + setup refresh note when assets ship
   - `## Added` / `## Fixed` / `## Changed` as needed (from `CHANGELOG.md`)
   - `## Upgrade` with the usual `hermes plugins update` / `gateway setup` / `restart` block
   - Link to `CHANGELOG.md` on the tag + compare URL
3. Prefer `gh release edit` (or `gh release create` with `--notes`) right after the tag push. If `gh` auth is broken, say so and ask — do not invent one-shot workflows unless the user wants that.
